# Store every text file with LF in the repository. Windows working copies still
# get CRLF where the platform expects it, via core.autocrlf on checkout.
* text=auto

# Scripts stay LF even in a Windows working copy.
#
# The CI model cache keys off hashFiles('build/download-test-models.ps1'), and
# hashFiles reads the working tree, not the stored blob. Under text=auto alone a
# Windows runner would check the script out as CRLF, compute a different key
# from the Linux job that populated the cache, miss it, and re-download the
# models on every build. PowerShell and bash both handle LF on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Test corpora are data under test, not source: they are copied from
# opennlp-tools/src/test/resources verbatim, and the readers under test are line
# oriented. conll2003-en.sample ships with CRLF terminators upstream while its
# siblings use LF, and that mix is part of what the ported tests read. Normalizing
# it under text=auto would silently change the bytes a parser sees, and would make
# the fixture differ from the Apache OpenNLP release this port targets.
src/NOpenNLP.Tools.Tests/Formats/**/*.sample -text
src/NOpenNLP.Tools.Tests/Formats/*.sample -text
src/NOpenNLP.Tools.Tests/Formats/**/*.ann -text
src/NOpenNLP.Tools.Tests/Formats/**/*.conllu -text
src/NOpenNLP.Tools.Tests/Formats/**/*.sgml -text
src/NOpenNLP.Tools.Tests/Formats/Brat/*.txt -text
src/NOpenNLP.Tools.Tests/Formats/Leipzig/** -text

# Never touch the bytes of binary files.
*.bin binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.snk binary
